// TEST: Tuple Equality Component Unit Mismatch (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3006
// ERROR-CONTAINS: meters / seconds vs meters
// ============================================================================
// The units discipline reaches INSIDE the tuple. `IR.getUnits` reads the top
// of a type and an `IRTTuple` carries no annotation there, so the whole-operand
// unit rule that guards a scalar comparison saw two unannotated values and
// waved this through: `(4.0 mps, 1) == (4.0 meters, 1)` type-checked, compiled,
// and printed `true` on the strength of the bare number 4.0 appearing on both
// sides. Exactly the class of plausible-but-wrong the unit system exists to
// refuse -- and the same one-level component descent `017` added for the
// direct-call argument seam.
//
// The comparison rule itself is unchanged (`unitRulesForOp`, "comparison"),
// applied once per component pair instead of once per operand.
// ============================================================================
Unit meters
Unit seconds
Unit mps = meters / seconds
let speed = 4.0: Float<mps>
let dist = 4.0: Float<meters>
let t1 = speed, 1
let t2 = dist, 1
let r = t1 == t2
// EXPECT: typecheck failure -- mps and meters are not comparable
